1. **I. G has a vertex with no incoming edge**:
   In a DAG, there must be at least one vertex with no incoming edges. This is because if every vertex had at least one incoming edge, we would have a cycle (since the graph is finite and directed), which contradicts the acyclic property. So **I is true**.

