   An isolated vertex is one with neither incoming nor outgoing edges. While it is possible for a DAG to have isolated vertices (vertices with no edges at all), it is not *necessary*. A DAG can exist without isolated vertices (e.g., a simple path or a tree). So **III is not necessarily true**.

